      "comment": "A risky one, admittedly, but sits on a lovely mark with a nice weight, with the jockey taking off a further 5 lbs also. He's a course regular here. He also won this race off a mark of 103 back in 2023. He runs off just 92 today. That's without accounting for the extra 5 lbs the jockey takes off with his claim. He won at this track around this time last year as well off a higher mark than this. He beat O'Connell comfortably. That rates decent form when you consider the runner-up is now rated 132 and placed in the Eider off that mark last time out. He qualified for this with a fair run last time out, beaten 8L behind Red Happy back in 4th place. To be fair, the ground was far too quick for him on that occasion. The blinkers are left on again this time, having run well in first-time blinkers last time out."
